@@ -3,7 +3,11 @@
 Client for `inventory-api`. Every function takes a `transport`,
 `async (request) => response`, so callers choose HTTP, IPC or a fake.
 
-- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `listItems(transport)` → every item, ordered by `id`. The API pages its
+  results, so this requests `/items` repeatedly, passing each response's
+  `next_cursor` back as `cursor` until it is `null` (or absent). It rejects on
+  any non-200 response, on a body without an `items` array, and when the server
+  returns the same `next_cursor` twice.
 - `getItem(transport, id)` → one item; rejects on any non-200 response.
 - `lowStock(items, threshold)` → SKUs with `qty` below the threshold.
 
